# ai-call-center-supervisor — copy to .env and adjust.
# ../lib/resolve-env.sh loads this file automatically from run.sh.

# Provisioning is now declarative — see manifest.yaml + README.md's
# "Provision (declarative)" section. Editing the LLM provider/model,
# connector, hosted CRM service, Telegram recipient (systemVariables), or
# workflow shape happens in manifest.yaml, NOT via env vars (the vars below
# only affect run.sh/src/index.ts's read-only driver, which posts two sample
# messages through the already-provisioned instance — it never creates or
# modifies platform objects).

# The secret VALUE for the LLM connector's bearer auth, read verbatim by
# --secrets-from-env (the binding name IS the env var name, no transform).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ----- Names run.sh/src/index.ts look up (must match manifest.yaml if overridden) ---
SUPERVISOR_WORKFLOW_NAME=ai-call-center-supervisor
AI_AGENT_NAME=ai-sample-supervisor
SUPERVISOR_HTTP_EXTERNAL_ID=manifest:ai-call-center-supervisor

# ----- Gateway / tenant (resolved automatically; override only if needed) ------------
# YOIZEN_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
# YOIZEN_HOST_HEADER=api-gateway.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# YOIZEN_TENANT=acme
# YOIZEN_EMAIL=yclawd@demo.io
# YOIZEN_PASSWORD=admin123

# --- run.sh knobs ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPERVISOR_RUN_TEXT_ANGRY=third time my bill is wrong, I want a $200 refund or I cancel
# SUPERVISOR_RUN_TEXT_CALM=how do I update my email address?
# SUPERVISOR_RUN_PAUSE_SECONDS=3
